Introduction

ASML is an innovation leader in the semiconductor industry. We provide chipmakers with sophisticated hardware to achieve lithographic patterning of several nm-size microchip features. The unprecedented precision and accuracy of our tools would not be possible without highly advanced optical measurement systems. Therefore, ASML Research continuously explores novel methods to generate, manipulate, illuminate, and measure light at wavelengths across the electromagnetic spectrum.

Your Assignment

ASML Research offers various internship opportunities. Your internship may be more theoretical (analytical / numerical) or experimental, depending on your preferences. You will work in a multidisciplinary team of experts with access to experimental setups, where theoretical insights can be explored in practice. During your internship assignment, you may work on one or more of the topics below:

Apply your theoretical knowledge to optimize properties of optical systems and photonics;

Explore novel optical metrology concepts; 

Investigate new light sources and detectors;

Develop analytical and/or numerical physical models to understand the behaviour of advanced light sources;

Design and conduct experiments, interpret results and communicate findings;

Support setup automations to enable efficient measurements;

Design integrated photonic devices using commercial design software;

We offer Master's apprentice or thesis internships, requiring a commitment of 4-5 days a week, with a duration of 5 to 12 months. The internship content, start date and duration can be discussed during the interview. ASML provides internship compensation and if you receive an offer, you will be informed about it.

Your Profile

To be a fit for an internship at ASML Research, you:

Have experience with 1) physical modelling and Fourier analysis or 2) optical experiments and hardware control, or 3) optical simulation software;

Have knowledge of programming languages such as Mathematica, MATLAB, Python, or LabVIEW;

Are currently a Master's student in Physics, Optics, Photonics, or a related field;

Are a committed individual with problem-solving and communication skills;

Are advanced in spoken and written English.

Bear in mind that the recruitment process takes longer for this position as multiple stakeholders are involved in the review stage. 

Eligibility requirements you need to meet:

You are enrolled at an educational institute for the entire duration of the internship;

You are located in the Netherlands to perform your internship. In case you are currently living/studying outside of the Netherlands, your CV/motivation letter includes willingness to relocate;

If you are a non-EU citizen, studying in the Netherlands, your university is willing to sign the documents required for doing an internship (i.e., Nuffic agreement).

This position requires access to controlled technology, as defined in the United States Export Administration Regulations (15 C.F.R. § 730, et seq.). Qualified candidates must be legally authorized to access such controlled technology prior to beginning work. Business demands may require ASML to proceed with candidates who are immediately eligible to access controlled technology.

